 experiences of psychiatric nurses in the United States</article-title><source>Nurs Stand</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>38</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050005-b034"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>They are more than just pretty people handing out cool pens</article-title><source>Dermatol Nurs</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>324</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16948376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050005-b035"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Dispensing pharmaceutical samples: A few reminders</article-title><source>Nurse Pract</source><volume>31</volume><fpage>15</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16607206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050005-b036"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Alexander-Banys</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Pharmaceutical company advertising practices: Call to arms</article-title><source>J Pediatr Health Care</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11904637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050005-b037"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Sidiqi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Edmunds</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Pharmaceutical influence</article-title><source>Nurse Pract</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>6</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12792263</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0050005-b038"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Edmunds</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article